## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> The current `hybrid_rag/reranker.py` uses `BGEM3FlagModel` (bi-encoder multi-head) as a reranker — NOT `bge-reranker-v2-m3`. This means the "generic reranker" baseline in Script 3 must be `BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3` (cross-encoder, out of the box), while the existing pipeline uses a completely different model. Script 3 will compare:
> - **Generic**: `BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3` (cross-encoder, no fine-tuning) → this establishes the 92.91% baseline
> - **Fine-tuned**: `./reranker_finetuned` (cross-encoder, fine-tuned on legal data)
>
> Script 4 will also **replace** the BGE-M3 unified multi-head model with the fine-tuned cross-encoder. This changes the reranker architecture entirely.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The prompt template for `bge-reranker-v2-m3` during inference: the FlagEmbedding library automatically prepends `"Represent this sentence for searching relevant passages: "` to the query. During training pair construction (Script 1/2), we must use the **same prefix** so training and inference are consistent. This is handled in Script 2 during tokenization.

